Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.45,0:00:30.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Dearest gentle reader,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.83,0:00:33.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must send felicitations{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.46,0:00:36.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to the new Duke and Duchess of Hastings.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.38,0:00:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Congratulations and stamina{\i0}\N{\i1}as they embark{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.71,0:00:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}on the most exhilarating time{\i0}\N{\i1}in a young couple's life.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.89,0:00:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am, of course, talking of the honeymoon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.27,0:00:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horses neighing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.08,0:01:21.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is there a more romantic notion?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.50,0:01:25.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-To retreat from society together…{\i0}\N<span style="style1">-Good morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.22,0:01:28.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-…finally leaving watchful eyes behind.{\i0}\N<span style="style1">-Good morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.89,0:01:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Welcome to Clyvedon, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.27,0:01:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It has been so long{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.77,0:01:41.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}since we have been blessed{\i0}\N{\i1}with your presence,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.69,0:01:43.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I trust{\i0}\N{\i1}you will find everything to your liking.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.78,0:01:46.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not doubt it, Mrs. Colson.{\i0}\N{\i1}I hope you have been well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.32,0:01:47.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.24,0:01:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}May I introduce to you{\i0}\N{\i1}the Duchess of Hastings?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.70,0:01:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am looking forward{\i0}\N{\i1}to making your acquaintance, Mrs. Colson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.58,0:01:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.29,0:01:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have planned everything{\i0}\N{\i1}to make you both comfortable.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.00,0:02:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}First, a light meal,{\i0}\N{\i1}served on the terrace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.50,0:02:03.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then a tour to show you{\i0}\N{\i1}all the improvements I have made. Then--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.50,0:02:06.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure it will be most diverting,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I am afraid it will have to wait.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.63,0:02:09.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have plans of my own for my new bride.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.09,0:02:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.80,0:02:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.65,0:02:21.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.86,0:02:23.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want to show you the bedroom.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.57,0:02:26.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yours or mine?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.36,0:02:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You truly believe{\i0}\N{\i1}we are to have separate rooms?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.99,0:02:31.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should think not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.36,0:02:33.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both chuckling] Stop! They shall see!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.45,0:02:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever will they think?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.20,0:02:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does it matter?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.04,0:02:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.45,0:02:39.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.54,0:02:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}<span style="style2"> While this author,{\i0}\N<span style="style2">along with the rest of the ton,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.54,0:02:47.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}will certainly miss{\i0}\N{\i1}its most-remarked-upon couple{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.88,0:02:48.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}back in London,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.01,0:02:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}perhaps we might find solace{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.76,0:02:56.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in the promise of the duke and duchess{\i0}\N{\i1}returning to us bearing a surprise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.26,0:02:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.56,0:03:00.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder what Daphne is doing{\i0}\N{\i1}at this very moment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.06,0:03:04.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure she has many new duties{\i0}\N{\i1}to attend to as duchess,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.19,0:03:05.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}things you should be learning{\i0}\N{\i1}for your debut.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.98,0:03:06.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise scoffs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.94,0:03:08.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Making simpering conversation,{\i0}\N{\i1}pretending not to wince{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.86,0:03:10.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}every time a man treads{\i0}\N{\i1}on my toes during a waltz?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.70,0:03:12.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Eloise!{\i0}\N{\i1}-I'm no good at those things.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.24,0:03:13.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll only make a fool of myself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.66,0:03:15.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you devoted as much time{\i0}\N{\i1}to your deportment lessons{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.99,0:03:18.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as you did to writing in your journal,{\i0}\N{\i1}you might feel rather better.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.66,0:03:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And on that subject,{\i0}\N{\i1}in preparation for your season,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.04,0:03:23.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it is time we lowered your skirts{\i0}\N{\i1}to wear at home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.33,0:03:25.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have no time{\i0}\N{\i1}for a visit to the modiste.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.13,0:03:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am busy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.21,0:03:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The queen herself has charged me{\i0}\N{\i1}with discovering Whistledown's identity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.13,0:03:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You would not have me cross{\i0}\N{\i1}Her Majesty, would you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.51,0:03:34.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[glass clanging]{\i0}\N{\i1}-May I have everyone's attention?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.97,0:03:40.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would like to make a small{\i0}\N{\i1}but important announcement.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.44,0:03:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have happy news to impart.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.27,0:03:50.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have asked Miss Marina Thompson{\i0}\N{\i1}to be my wife, and she has accepted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.86,0:03:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests exclaim happily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.95,0:03:54.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[applause]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.04,0:04:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[woman] Congratulations!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.33,0:04:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests laughing, chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.79,0:04:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[man] Bravo, sir!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.88,0:04:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you know about this?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.55,0:04:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}People are looking, dear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.92,0:04:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Congratulate the happy couple.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.85,0:04:23.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You barely know the young lady.{\i0}\N{\i1}What were you thinking?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.06,0:04:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was thinking you'd respond like this{\i0}\N{\i1}and how little I would care to hear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.06,0:04:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you think this is a joke?{\i0}\N{\i1}Poor Mother was beside herself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.77,0:04:32.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mother seems perfectly happy to me.{\i0}\N{\i1}She congratulated us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.78,0:04:36.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So, you compromised this young lady?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.11,0:04:38.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Certainly not. I am a gentleman.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Then why ever would you--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.03,0:04:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why does anyone marry, brother?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.49,0:04:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For love, of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.58,0:04:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look, I know you are still rather green,{\i0}\N{\i1}and that is my fault.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.87,0:04:49.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should've taken you to brothels{\i0}\N{\i1}when you returned from Eton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.34,0:04:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If this is a matter{\i0}\N{\i1}of wetting your wick--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.17,0:04:52.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are an ass. Do you know that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.63,0:04:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is what comes{\i0}\N{\i1}of not sowing your wild oats.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.26,0:04:57.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Proposing to the first chit{\i0}\N{\i1}you set your cap at.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.26,0:04:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Enough!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.26,0:05:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You insult me and my intended.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.31,0:05:05.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is not my fault, nor Marina's,{\i0}\N{\i1}that you cannot fathom true attachment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.35,0:05:09.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You are still a child, Colin.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I'm older than Daphne.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.23,0:05:11.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You were happy to marry her off.{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is not the same.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.44,0:05:14.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I know nothing of the sort.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Then you betray your immaturity!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.90,0:05:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If{\i0}<span style="style2"> {\i0}{\i1}I caused Mother discomfort today,{\i0}\N{\i1}I am sorry for it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.41,0:05:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall speak with her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.78,0:05:24.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The truth is, I do not require{\i0}\N{\i1}your permission to marry Miss Thompson…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.00,0:05:28.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I would very much prefer{\i0}\N{\i1}to have your blessing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.92,0:05:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then I am afraid I must disappoint you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.71,0:05:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.21,0:05:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in more ways than one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.05,0:05:39.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens, closes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.80,0:05:41.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[theme music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.06,0:05:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}I believe I now know the reason{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.27,0:05:54.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}why every mama of the ton keeps{\i0}\N{\i1}her daughter in total darkness{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.53,0:05:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}about certain… diversions.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.65,0:05:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.11,0:06:00.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.20,0:06:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] Should they have told us{\i0}\N{\i1}what it was truly like,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.45,0:06:06.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}however would we get{\i0}\N{\i1}anything else done at all?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.45,0:06:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.62,0:06:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Simon kissing]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[moans lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.54,0:06:12.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I must go.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.75,0:06:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I am to be duchess of all of this,{\i0}\N{\i1}I must start learning the lie of the land.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.42,0:06:18.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are already duchess of all this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.88,0:06:20.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Simon chuckles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-And I look forward{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.51,0:06:23.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to exploring that particular land further…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.72,0:06:26.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Later.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.31,0:06:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simon!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.35,0:06:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You said the duchy was most intimidating.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.52,0:06:34.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why not stay and lord it over this room?{\i0}\N{\i1}You may find it a bit more titillating.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.73,0:06:36.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[laughs] I do not doubt it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.07,0:06:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I suspect{\i0}\N{\i1}Mrs. Colson shall always resent me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.53,0:06:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if I do not take her tour.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.99,0:06:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[whispering] Then let her resent.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.87,0:06:44.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon moans lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.95,0:06:47.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall do nothing of the sort.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.12,0:06:50.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My mother told me a lady is nothing{\i0}\N{\i1}without her housekeeper.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.71,0:06:52.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must make a good impression,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.92,0:06:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or nothing{\i0}\N{\i1}in this house shall run smoothly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.17,0:07:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then I wish you well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.55,0:07:04.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Your Grace.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.72,0:07:05.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.89,0:07:08.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens, closes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.98,0:07:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[knocking, door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.44,0:07:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have prepared the study{\i0}\N{\i1}for you to work, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.32,0:07:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Jeffries, I am on my honeymoon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.86,0:07:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The steward has left the records{\i0}\N{\i1}in some disarray.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.78,0:07:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot make head nor tail{\i0}\N{\i1}of the estate's accounting,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.74,0:07:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and there are several letters{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.28,0:07:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from farm tenants begging{\i0}\N{\i1}an audience with Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.91,0:07:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very well! [groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.75,0:07:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I must.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.75,0:07:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The castle was built in 1706{\i0}\N{\i1}for Admiral Thomas,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.17,0:07:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a gift from Her Majesty Queen Anne--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.72,0:07:45.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For his military triumphs{\i0}\N{\i1}against the French, I believe.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.43,0:07:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My younger sister Hyacinth{\i0}\N{\i1}is something of a student of history.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.39,0:07:51.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very well, Your Grace. Here we are.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.89,0:07:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The morning room,{\i0}\N{\i1}where the former duchess{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.02,0:07:55.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}preferred to take tea with visitors.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.69,0:07:59.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My mama suggested{\i0}\N{\i1}I extend an invitation to the vicar first.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.61,0:08:02.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I believe she is right.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Of course, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.49,0:08:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I look forward to hosting our first ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.20,0:08:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I believe it would be prudent to wait{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.49,0:08:10.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}until after the close{\i0}\N{\i1}of the London season, yes?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.37,0:08:12.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Indeed, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.71,0:08:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.67,0:08:17.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I shall look{\i0}\N{\i1}at redecorating this room first.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.46,0:08:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You wish to redecorate?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.09,0:08:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Certainly, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.26,0:08:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is to be a fair{\i0}\N{\i1}in the village this week.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.59,0:08:27.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I offered it patronage on your behalf.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.89,0:08:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Most thoughtful of you, Mrs. Colson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.77,0:08:33.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps we might give the servants{\i0}\N{\i1}some time off to attend as well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.43,0:08:34.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is much to be done{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.98,0:08:37.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}now that the duke{\i0}\N{\i1}and yourself are in residence.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.27,0:08:40.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ah. Well, even more reason{\i0}\N{\i1}to allow them some respite, then.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.36,0:08:44.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that…?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.70,0:08:47.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The former duchess, yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.20,0:08:49.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-She was beautiful.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Thoughtful, too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.78,0:08:50.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Most proper.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.83,0:08:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A perfect duchess.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.46,0:08:55.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.46,0:09:05.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And here is the nursery.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.06,0:09:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.22,0:09:14.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.93,0:09:16.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-It is lovely.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.23,0:09:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shall we move on?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.15,0:09:22.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am certain there is much left to see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.28,0:09:24.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, of course.{\i0}\N{\i1}Let me show you your grounds.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.17,0:09:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] My apologies. I--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.59,0:09:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are we expecting royalty?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.13,0:09:50.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Begging your pardon, Your Grace.{\i0}\N{\i1}The late duke preferred a formal table.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.51,0:09:54.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-But if you prefer--{\i0}\N{\i1}-No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.64,0:09:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, never mind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.57,0:10:08.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mrs. Colson's tour today was exceptional.{\i0}\N{\i1}The gardens are particularly lovely.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.90,0:10:12.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I found myself{\i0}\N{\i1}in continual awe of their beauty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.37,0:10:17.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is anything wrong?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.79,0:10:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[scoffs] You…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.79,0:10:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are so far away.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.33,0:10:23.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.71,0:10:25.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, that is easily remedied.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.96,0:10:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is no trouble, truly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.55,0:10:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.39,0:10:32.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.02,0:10:45.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There, now. Much better, yes?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.07,0:10:50.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought perhaps{\i0}\N{\i1}to redecorate a few rooms{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.70,0:10:52.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but wished to talk to you first.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.49,0:10:55.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'd hate to change anything{\i0}\N{\i1}you're particularly attached to.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.37,0:10:57.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then you may change it all.{\i0}\N{\i1}In fact, please do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.95,0:10:59.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] Now, do not jest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.96,0:11:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must have fond memories…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.46,0:11:05.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or sentimental attachments.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.46,0:11:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After all,{\i0}\N{\i1}this has been your home for many years.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.01,0:11:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do what you will.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.13,0:11:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Paper the drawing room{\i0}\N{\i1}in flamingo-pink tulle.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.01,0:11:12.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure I shall love it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.39,0:11:15.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do know,{\i0}\N{\i1}you need not dress so formally here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.43,0:11:22.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does this meet your approval?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.19,0:11:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, without question.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.19,0:11:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.65,0:11:30.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.65,0:11:33.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace, should we…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.95,0:11:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}go upstairs?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.24,0:11:37.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have a better idea.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.49,0:11:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.67,0:11:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where are we going?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.25,0:11:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.38,0:11:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.14,0:11:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[thunder crackles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.77,0:12:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.99,0:12:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.59,0:12:37.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasping, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.69,0:12:46.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you like this?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.44,0:12:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell me what you want.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.27,0:12:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[shuddering breaths]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.11,0:12:53.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.36,0:12:57.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.79,0:13:08.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[thunder booms]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.79,0:13:11.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both gasping, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.39,0:13:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne moaning loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.44,0:13:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[laughs, panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.86,0:13:36.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.03,0:13:39.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does that hurt?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.57,0:13:41.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[laughs]{\i0}\N{\i1}-When you…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.83,0:13:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.29,0:13:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I feel as you feel,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.54,0:13:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}absolutely wonderful.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.34,0:13:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[classical music playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.90,0:14:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[classical music continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.07,0:14:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.16,0:14:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[moaning lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.54,0:14:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.83,0:14:31.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wait!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.75,0:14:34.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wait! Come here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.75,0:14:38.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.47,0:14:40.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Whatever will the staff think?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Does it matter?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.47,0:14:46.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[muffled grunting, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.02,0:14:55.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[muffled moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.36,0:14:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[glass shatters]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.90,0:14:58.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[moaning continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.55,0:15:25.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Ah!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Ooh.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.76,0:15:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Apologies, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.52,0:15:33.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, our activities are quite… spirited.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.94,0:15:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I admit,{\i0}\N{\i1}I did not even know it was possible.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.65,0:15:44.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believed his physical inability{\i0}\N{\i1}to have children would preclude him from…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.41,0:15:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…causing such difficult entanglements?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.16,0:15:49.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both giggling]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.95,0:15:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.83,0:15:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am quite glad to say I was wrong.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.29,0:15:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laugh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.38,0:15:59.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both sigh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.31,0:16:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict] He took your ribbon?{\i0}\N{\i1}Did you take the ribbon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.56,0:16:13.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Gregory] Dunno what you're talking ab--{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Hyacinth] I saw him do it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.31,0:16:15.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Benedict] I saw it in your pocket.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Hyacinth] It's not fair.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.94,0:16:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He does it every time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.06,0:16:18.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Just give it back.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Gregory, stop!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.90,0:16:19.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Good morning.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Greg--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.82,0:16:22.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Morning, brother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.99,0:16:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Colin, your engagement is in Whistledown!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Hyacinth!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.28,0:16:28.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Hyacinth] What? It is!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.99,0:16:31.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Very well. Everyone out, I think.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Violet] Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.72,0:16:43.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did say I was sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.80,0:16:46.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose I ought to be relieved{\i0}\N{\i1}I found out before Lady Whistledown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.93,0:16:49.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mother, I have been courting{\i0}\N{\i1}Miss Thompson all season.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.85,0:16:52.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you were so taken up by Daphne{\i0}\N{\i1}you failed to see it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.35,0:16:56.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew you were flirting with her,{\i0}\N{\i1}but you flirt with plenty of young ladies.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.19,0:16:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You always have, never in earnest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.31,0:17:01.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Until now.{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is all happening so quickly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.69,0:17:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am not sure I have ever seen you{\i0}\N{\i1}so solemn and serious.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.41,0:17:09.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No one ever takes me seriously,{\i0}\N{\i1}except Marina.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.20,0:17:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was not prepared to let{\i0}\N{\i1}another of you fly the nest so soon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.96,0:17:18.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Never fear, Mother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.04,0:17:20.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will still have your hands full.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.05,0:17:24.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Especially with Eloise.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.05,0:17:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good luck with that one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.34,0:17:30.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horses neighing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.14,0:17:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you think{\i0}\N{\i1}Colin will introduce us to his friends?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.85,0:17:36.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Some of them are quite strapping.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I am sure he will.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.27,0:17:38.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure all of our fortunes{\i0}\N{\i1}are about to change.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.90,0:17:40.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm. Especially Colin's.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.65,0:17:46.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You look very lovely today, Penelope.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Do not mock me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.08,0:17:56.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It pains me you should think{\i0}\N{\i1}every compliment a mockery.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.91,0:17:58.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do not pity me, either.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.50,0:18:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not pity you, Penelope.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.08,0:18:01.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I respect you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.46,0:18:05.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have been a true friend{\i0}\N{\i1}since I arrived here,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.55,0:18:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I rely on your continued friendship{\i0}\N{\i1}and sympathy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.47,0:18:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My continued silence, you mean?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.43,0:18:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You think so little of me,{\i0}\N{\i1}I cannot bear it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.89,0:18:18.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I never would have made my way{\i0}\N{\i1}through this awful tangle{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.73,0:18:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}without your kindness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.85,0:18:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please do not tell me you regret it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.57,0:18:26.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would never bring scandal{\i0}\N{\i1}on you or our family,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.61,0:18:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if that is what you ask,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.11,0:18:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I cannot condone your actions.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.16,0:18:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want you as my friend, Pen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.20,0:18:38.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Can you not try to understand{\i0}\N{\i1}and be a little pleased for me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.41,0:18:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina? Time for the modiste.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.38,0:18:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We must see to your trousseau.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.26,0:18:52.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[scoffs] She is so lucky.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Prudence sighs wistfully]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.01,0:18:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A whole new wardrobe{\i0}\N{\i1}and a handsome husband.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.89,0:18:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Between the two of them,{\i0}\N{\i1}they will make the most beautiful baby.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.73,0:19:03.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is not the father, you dunderhead!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.48,0:19:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[both laughing]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh, my goodness! I clean forgot.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.44,0:19:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do not laugh at him!{\i0}\N{\i1}She makes a fool of him already.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.19,0:19:11.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ugh! You are no fun anymore.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.12,0:19:14.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Was I ever?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.54,0:19:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}See? You will look so very lovely{\i0}\N{\i1}with it pinned up next season.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.04,0:19:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No. I will look like{\i0}\N{\i1}every other young lady,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.08,0:19:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}except less graceful{\i0}\N{\i1}and more bad-tempered.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.71,0:19:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Bridgerton. Miss Eloise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.22,0:19:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I understand we are here{\i0}\N{\i1}on the matter of dropping our hems?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.39,0:19:34.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Precisely.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.10,0:19:38.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Featherington]{\i0}\N{\i1}Lady Bridgerton! There you are.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.60,0:19:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Featherington. Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.85,0:19:42.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is lovely to see you, Lady Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.02,0:19:45.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must call me Violet now, I insist.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.86,0:19:47.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is this not just delightful,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.69,0:19:51.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to know now{\i0}\N{\i1}that our families will be joined forever?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.20,0:19:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, it certainly is something.{\i0}\N{\i1}[strained chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.70,0:19:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must join us tomorrow night,{\i0}\N{\i1}you, and dear Colin, and the viscount.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.58,0:20:02.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-We have so much to celebrate.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I will certainly ask the viscount.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.50,0:20:06.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perfect. Now, I shall need to steal{\i0}\N{\i1}Madame Delacroix away for a moment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.63,0:20:10.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] I do apologize,{\i0}\N{\i1}Lady Featherington,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.71,0:20:12.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but first there is the matter{\i0}\N{\i1}of your account.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.97,0:20:15.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was clear to your maid{\i0}\N{\i1}that your line of credit--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.09,0:20:16.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Allow me to stop you there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.56,0:20:21.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our bills will be settled in full{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.39,0:20:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as soon as you have made Miss Thompson,{\i0}\N{\i1}soon-to-be Bridgerton,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.94,0:20:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}her gown{\i0}\N{\i1}and the other items for her trousseau.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.23,0:20:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am afraid that is not possible.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.86,0:20:33.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you might find another tailoress{\i0}\N{\i1}more to your liking across town.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.78,0:20:36.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Oui?{\i0}\N<span style="style1">-Madame Delacroix, that reminds me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.45,0:20:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have such a unique accent,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.12,0:20:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and yet I have never asked{\i0}\N{\i1}where in France you're from.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.75,0:20:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[in French]{\i0}\N{\i1}My mother was French, you see,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.17,0:20:47.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I am not fooled by your little act.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.17,0:20:50.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would hate{\i0}\N{\i1}for the other ladies of the ton{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.42,0:20:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to learn they have been taken in as well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.67,0:20:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[in English] I believe Madame Delacroix{\i0}\N{\i1}will be somewhat more amenable{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.72,0:21:00.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to our requests now, Lady Featherington.{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Très bon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.64,0:21:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Très bon.{\i0}\N<span style="style1">-[Marina] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.86,0:21:16.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[attendees chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.74,0:21:19.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[pigs snorting loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.62,0:21:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is the prize for the winner?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.08,0:21:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why, slaughter, of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.00,0:21:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.17,0:21:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Simon clears throat]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Daphne] Ahem.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.30,0:21:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As the duke has granted me the honor{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.63,0:21:40.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of opening our village fair{\i0}\N{\i1}with this contest,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.26,0:21:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it is after careful consideration{\i0}\N{\i1}that I have decided…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.73,0:21:48.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that all three pigs have tied!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.77,0:21:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[confused murmuring]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.98,0:21:54.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hereby decree every pig such a winner{\i0}\N{\i1}that none should be slaughtered.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.11,0:21:59.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[hesitant applause]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.16,0:22:05.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[maypole dance music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.46,0:22:10.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They look lovely.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.79,0:22:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look at those.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.75,0:22:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why, these are delicious!{\i0}\N{\i1}We must order some for Clyvedon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.97,0:22:21.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does your patronage extend{\i0}\N{\i1}beyond pies, Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.80,0:22:26.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The harvests on the farm have been poor,{\i0}\N{\i1}and with the rents being tripled,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.81,0:22:28.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}we are struggling{\i0}\N{\i1}to put food on the table.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.81,0:22:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The rents tripled?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.06,0:22:31.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My steward did not inform me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.61,0:22:33.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He hasn't shown his face{\i0}\N{\i1}since your father passed,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.69,0:22:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}God rest His Grace's soul.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.90,0:22:39.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He always gave his tenants{\i0}\N{\i1}what they needed, unlike some.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.28,0:22:42.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then it is a good thing indeed{\i0}\N{\i1}that we are back at Clyvedon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.12,0:22:45.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure we can find a solution{\i0}\N{\i1}to these difficulties,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.49,0:22:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I thank you{\i0}\N{\i1}for bringing them to our attention.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.08,0:22:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.50,0:22:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[child whining]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.92,0:22:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[child screeching, crying]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.17,0:23:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, there, there, there, child.{\i0}\N{\i1}No need to cry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.84,0:23:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}All is well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.51,0:23:07.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My! You have a strong set of lungs.{\i0}\N{\i1}They shall hear you all the way in London.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.60,0:23:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-If not all the way to France.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Daphne chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.44,0:23:12.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, my goodness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.77,0:23:14.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must apologize, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.44,0:23:16.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Little Ada{\i0}\N{\i1}has just discovered her own voice{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.73,0:23:19.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and likes to use it{\i0}\N{\i1}as often and loudly as she can.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.49,0:23:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, um…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.61,0:23:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, please, stand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.07,0:23:26.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should not be stooping{\i0}\N{\i1}in your condition.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.46,0:23:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, it was lovely{\i0}\N{\i1}to make your acquaintance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.04,0:23:38.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ada. [chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.34,0:23:39.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.71,0:23:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.26,0:23:44.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.39,0:23:52.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What can we do about the farmer's rent?{\i0}\N{\i1}There must be something.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.52,0:23:54.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should have returned sooner{\i0}\N{\i1}to see that things were in order.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.06,0:23:57.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not realize{\i0}\N{\i1}my absence would be felt this way.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.15,0:23:58.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Daphne--{\i0}\N{\i1}-I hope that--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.53,0:24:00.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.28,0:24:02.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I only meant to say,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.16,0:24:07.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hope it did not pain you too much{\i0}\N{\i1}to see me with those children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.99,0:24:09.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pain {\i0}<span style="style2">me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.29,0:24:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne, I thought only of you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.17,0:24:16.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know, oddly enough,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.96,0:24:18.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when I am actually{\i0}\N{\i1}in the presence of children,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.92,0:24:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I forget all about my own concerns.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.92,0:24:23.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They are the easiest company in the world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.01,0:24:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are natural with them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.18,0:24:27.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My younger sisters and brother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.89,0:24:30.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Each one a mischief.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.98,0:24:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know, my abundant family will be good{\i0}\N{\i1}for at least one thing in future.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.31,0:24:39.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eventually, they will all marry{\i0}\N{\i1}and have children of their own,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.82,0:24:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and we will have more screaming infants{\i0}\N{\i1}in our lives than we know what to do with.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.40,0:24:46.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.53,0:24:49.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will be a splendid aunt.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.41,0:24:54.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It thrills me that you are satisfied{\i0}\N{\i1}with our married life as it is,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.79,0:24:55.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}just the two of us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.50,0:24:58.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have all that I want just here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.17,0:25:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How did I earn such luck?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.51,0:25:03.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That I do not know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.82,0:25:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lord Featherington sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.70,0:25:31.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Turn, please.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.49,0:25:33.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Profile.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.12,0:25:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Swish.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:36.67,0:25:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Swish!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.34,0:25:45.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good. You have done well thus far,{\i0}\N{\i1}Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.88,0:25:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tonight, I shall need to raise{\i0}\N{\i1}the matter of a swift wedding.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.34,0:25:50.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[snickers loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.26,0:25:53.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.02,0:25:55.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}very sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.23,0:25:57.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But this plan of yours, I find it wanting.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.90,0:26:00.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Deceiving Colin is one thing,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.31,0:26:02.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but being at close quarters{\i0}\N{\i1}with his mother,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.90,0:26:03.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that is quite another.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.07,0:26:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Bridgerton is shrewd.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.49,0:26:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She has had eight children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.45,0:26:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Trust she knows when she is being managed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.58,0:26:15.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What were your favorite pastimes{\i0}\N{\i1}in the country?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.04,0:26:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I enjoyed riding above all else, my lady.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.67,0:26:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please,{\i0}\N{\i1}you must call me Violet now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.54,0:26:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Remember?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:21.46,0:26:24.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson{\i0}\N{\i1}is such a proper young lady, is she not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:24.75,0:26:27.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Have you traveled at all{\i0}\N{\i1}beyond England, Miss Thompson?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:27.67,0:26:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It has long been Colin's greatest ambition{\i0}\N{\i1}to travel the world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.14,0:26:32.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Never.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.72,0:26:35.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though it is now{\i0}\N{\i1}a great ambition of mine as well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.47,0:26:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sensing a honeymoon in foreign parts.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.69,0:26:41.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What think you, Lord Bridgerton?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:41.65,0:26:43.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would not like to speculate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.23,0:26:47.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, indeed. I believe a honeymoon{\i0}\N{\i1}in foreign parts would be just the thing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.28,0:26:49.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mr. Bridgerton,{\i0}\N{\i1}you might even make the most{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.57,0:26:51.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of this fine weather we've been having{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.28,0:26:54.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if you choose to marry{\i0}\N{\i1}sooner rather than later.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.41,0:26:57.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Colin is still very young.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.75,0:27:00.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe{\i0}\N{\i1}a lengthier engagement would be prudent,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.17,0:27:01.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}excellent weather notwithstanding.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.96,0:27:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mother, have I told you Miss Thompson{\i0}\N{\i1}is very accomplished at needlework?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.76,0:27:09.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She is quite brilliant.{\i0}\N{\i1}Puts my sisters to shame.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.92,0:27:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can assure you, that is not true.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.68,0:27:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have not seen{\i0}\N{\i1}my sister Daphne's embroidery.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.30,0:27:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-In all honesty, it is like a battlefield.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Lady Featerhington laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.64,0:27:19.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Marina chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.27,0:27:21.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Penelope slices loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.99,0:27:32.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[off-key]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">♪ Oh dear, what can the matter be? ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.66,0:27:36.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Oh dear, what can the matter be? ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.20,0:27:39.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Oh dear, what can the matter be? ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.70,0:27:42.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Johnny's so long at the fair ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.29,0:27:46.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ He promised he'd buy me{\i0}\N{\i1}A bunch of blue ribbons ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.92,0:27:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ He promised to buy me{\i0}\N{\i1}A bunch of blue ribbons ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.84,0:27:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Promised to buy me{\i0}\N{\i1}A bunch of blue ribbons ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:54.30,0:27:56.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ To tie up my bonny brown hair ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.43,0:27:58.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ And it's oh dear… ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.47,0:28:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Colin?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.77,0:28:02.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Might I have a word?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.77,0:28:03.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pen, of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.94,0:28:05.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Prudence] {\i0}<span style="style2">♪ What can the matter be ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.52,0:28:06.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Oh dear ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.77,0:28:08.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.61,0:28:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is a rather delicate matter.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.11,0:28:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wish I did not have cause to raise it,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I believe you deserve to know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.12,0:28:16.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is there something on my face?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.70,0:28:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Has it been there all evening?{\i0}\N{\i1}It has, hasn't it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.62,0:28:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sorry. Um, go on.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.04,0:28:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have wanted to talk to you{\i0}\N{\i1}since the engagement was announced,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.75,0:28:24.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but we're always in company.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.92,0:28:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So, this is something about Marina?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.50,0:28:28.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her heart belongs to another.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.21,0:28:30.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.13,0:28:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}His name is Sir George Crane.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.63,0:28:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is a first son, a soldier.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.22,0:28:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They grew up{\i0}\N{\i1}in neighboring properties in the country.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.43,0:28:37.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sorry,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I have seen their love letters.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.97,0:28:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I felt you should know{\i0}\N{\i1}before it was too late.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.15,0:28:46.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You really are very good. You know that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.52,0:28:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you think that I would care{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.90,0:28:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that she had fond feelings{\i0}\N{\i1}for another before we met?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.94,0:28:55.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It would be rich of me,{\i0}\N{\i1}considering I have flirted{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.20,0:28:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with half the girls in London{\i0}\N{\i1}at one point.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.12,0:29:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You misunderstand.{\i0}\N{\i1}This was no mere flirtation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:00.08,0:29:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina loves this man.{\i0}\N{\i1}She loves him still.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.08,0:29:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And yet she is marrying me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.71,0:29:05.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Trust me, Pen, do not fret.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.79,0:29:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know my mind and Marina's.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.67,0:29:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We understand each other.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.63,0:29:15.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh. Have we moved the party{\i0}\N{\i1}to the corridor?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.51,0:29:16.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know, it is peculiar,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.47,0:29:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but the further I get{\i0}\N{\i1}from that pianoforte,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.76,0:29:21.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the more like a party it feels.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.60,0:29:24.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pen, your mother's asking for you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:24.14,0:29:25.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[muffled music continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.31,0:29:30.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tepid applause]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.48,0:29:32.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Marina sighs deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.78,0:29:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is anything wrong?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:34.44,0:29:35.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it my brother? He…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.32,0:29:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He was odious at dinner. I apologize.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.53,0:29:40.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot stand it, Colin.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.62,0:29:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My own father does not want me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.08,0:29:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even the Featheringtons{\i0}\N{\i1}cannot wait to be rid of me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.71,0:29:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fool that I am, I truly thought{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.21,0:29:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that with your family,{\i0}\N{\i1}I might finally find acceptance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.50,0:29:52.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it is no use.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.96,0:29:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Even your mother is just being polite.{\i0}\N{\i1}-That is not true, Marina.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.93,0:30:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am your family now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.43,0:30:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We shall make our own family, you and me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.43,0:30:06.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is all I want.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.94,0:30:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is all I want in all the world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.48,0:30:12.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wish we could be married{\i0}\N{\i1}this very minute.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.98,0:30:15.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then we could be alone together always.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.74,0:30:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would never have to leave your arms.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.53,0:30:24.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What if I told you there was a way?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Colin, what are--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.20,0:30:26.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Scotland. Gretna Green.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.04,0:30:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know it is mad,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.50,0:30:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but we could be married{\i0}\N{\i1}within a matter of days.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.67,0:30:34.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We just have to make it to the border.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.21,0:30:37.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anthony would be an ogre about it{\i0}\N{\i1}when we first return, of course,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.17,0:30:38.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but by then, it would be too late.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:38.88,0:30:41.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We would be married. We would be together.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.31,0:30:45.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You hate the idea.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.73,0:30:48.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I love it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.52,0:30:50.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I love you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.98,0:30:54.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Allow me a day.{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall arrange everything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.15,0:30:56.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs happily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.91,0:31:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.70,0:31:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Ah. Here you are.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh, good morning, dearest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.70,0:31:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-The steward's books, I take it?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm. I could not sleep.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:52.29,0:31:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not even after last night's exertions?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.00,0:31:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.75,0:31:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you care to break your fast with me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:59.30,0:32:01.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sorry, my love.{\i0}\N{\i1}The farmer in the village was right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.63,0:32:03.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The estates have been neglected{\i0}\N{\i1}far too long.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.47,0:32:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wheat yields are down,{\i0}\N{\i1}yet nobody uses the fields{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:05.76,0:32:08.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for livestock grazing,{\i0}\N{\i1}or rotate to a more plentiful crop.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:08.60,0:32:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Is that not the steward's job?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[angrily] They're my tenants, my people.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:11.48,0:32:13.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The responsibility is mine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.69,0:32:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please, excuse me. I have been staring{\i0}\N{\i1}at these figures all morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:19.44,0:32:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:22.40,0:32:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose I have a good deal{\i0}\N{\i1}to occupy myself with today too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:25.70,0:32:26.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.91,0:32:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know,{\i0}\N{\i1}I mean to visit some of your tenants.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.41,0:32:32.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I might deliver some gift baskets and…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:43.17,0:32:44.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you missing home, Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.30,0:32:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you think we have enough{\i0}\N{\i1}for all the baskets?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.52,0:32:52.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Um, I should think so.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:53.06,0:32:54.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:54.98,0:32:56.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever are you…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.19,0:32:59.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will have someone{\i0}\N{\i1}gather those on your behalf.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:59.27,0:33:01.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}One of the kitchen maids or the gardener.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.44,0:33:03.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Was no one available to assist you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.24,0:33:05.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is no need{\i0}\N{\i1}to trouble anyone, Mrs. Colson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.70,0:33:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have it all in hand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.95,0:33:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you intend to collect honey{\i0}\N{\i1}from the hives in person as well?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.95,0:33:12.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] Oh…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.29,0:33:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That might be a little beyond me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.75,0:33:19.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you simply tell me{\i0}\N{\i1}of your wants and needs,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.17,0:33:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will ensure everything is in order.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.63,0:33:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will ensure everything is done properly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.43,0:33:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I shall keep that in mind.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.68,0:33:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you, Mrs. Colson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.93,0:33:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm-hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.60,0:33:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Faith, she despises me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:40.44,0:33:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She despises everybody.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.23,0:33:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do not give it another thought.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.11,0:33:45.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[villagers chattering, laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.57,0:33:48.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] Hello.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.57,0:33:49.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you like a basket?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.87,0:33:52.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-There is--{\i0}\N{\i1}-[villager clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:53.20,0:33:54.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A basket from Clyvedon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.71,0:33:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh! A basket from Clyvedon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.42,0:33:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-There is--{\i0}\N{\i1}-[villagers whisper, indistinct]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.17,0:34:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is something amiss?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.09,0:34:07.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama taught me it was tradition{\i0}\N{\i1}for the new duchess to visit with gifts.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:07.63,0:34:09.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I believe it is proper.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:10.05,0:34:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should I have worn a different dress?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.35,0:34:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or perhaps it signifies{\i0}\N{\i1}I am high in the instep.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.27,0:34:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Ada] Your Grace!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:17.23,0:34:18.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Ada laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.23,0:34:24.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you like a basket from Clyvedon?{\i0}\N{\i1}There is bread and honey for the children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:24.32,0:34:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh. You are too kind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.40,0:34:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would gladly take one{\i0}\N{\i1}if I had means to carry it home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.61,0:34:31.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then we are determined to walk with you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.49,0:34:32.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, no. I didn't--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:32.95,0:34:34.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I insist.{\i0}\N{\i1}-No. Oh, I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:35.45,0:34:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.25,0:34:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps I might ask{\i0}\N{\i1}your opinion on something?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.33,0:34:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.25,0:34:44.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though, how I might{\i0}\N{\i1}advise a duchess, I am not sure.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.59,0:34:48.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I feel that I have done something{\i0}\N{\i1}to offend the village.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.88,0:34:51.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know I am new to the role,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.43,0:34:54.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I cannot imagine{\i0}\N{\i1}what I have done wrong so soon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:57.02,0:34:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What?{\i0}\N{\i1}-It was the pigs.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.69,0:35:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You said that all three pigs won.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.06,0:35:04.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}At the fair?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:05.19,0:35:07.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought it the best outcome{\i0}\N{\i1}for everyone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.19,0:35:09.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is tradition that the winner is allowed{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.40,0:35:11.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to supply pork to Clyvedon{\i0}\N{\i1}for the next year.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.82,0:35:15.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's a great number of pigs, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.24,0:35:17.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When you could not choose a winner,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.79,0:35:19.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}no farmer won the contract,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.75,0:35:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}nor the income to go along with it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.67,0:35:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Daphne gasps]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Simply speaking, you, um…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:24.42,0:35:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You snubbed them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.84,0:35:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will correct my mistake at once. I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:28.80,0:35:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had no idea.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.26,0:35:32.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs] How could you have, Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.52,0:35:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is all this?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.28,0:35:48.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.36,0:35:49.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[man] Steady…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.32,0:35:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Is everything well?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Ah, Daphne. Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:51.40,0:35:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm setting up work in the east wing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.95,0:35:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What's wrong with the study?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[loud crash]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.66,0:35:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Careful!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.62,0:35:57.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You shall have to excuse me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.21,0:36:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.62,0:36:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mrs. Colson?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.25,0:36:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you have a moment?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.25,0:36:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Colson grunts lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:08.55,0:36:11.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know I have made some missteps{\i0}\N{\i1}since I arrived.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.55,0:36:15.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My mother taught me a great deal{\i0}\N{\i1}about being mistress of a household,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.55,0:36:17.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I am not sure{\i0}\N{\i1}either of us ever imagined{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.01,0:36:19.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a house as grand as this one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.81,0:36:20.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Colson] Mm-hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.27,0:36:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am so very grateful for your guidance,{\i0}\N{\i1}Mrs. Colson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.90,0:36:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The truth is…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.48,0:36:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I fear the duke might not{\i0}\N{\i1}be entirely at ease here at Clyvedon,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.11,0:36:35.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}which is of course no reflection{\i0}\N{\i1}of you or any of your staff.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.03,0:36:39.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-No. I-- I quite understand.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:39.33,0:36:40.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Master Simon--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.54,0:36:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eh… I beg your pardon. His Grace…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.33,0:36:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}His childhood was not always easy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.54,0:36:48.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After the death of my late mistress,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.46,0:36:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the duke lived almost exclusively{\i0}\N{\i1}in London.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.71,0:36:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you mean to say{\i0}\N{\i1}that Simon grew up here on his own?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.13,0:36:54.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We did our best to take care of him,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.76,0:36:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to mind him{\i0}\N{\i1}as his mother would have wanted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.59,0:36:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course you did.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:57.76,0:36:58.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Colson] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:00.10,0:37:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The late duke{\i0}\N{\i1}must have loved his wife very much{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.06,0:37:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to have struggled so after her death.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.06,0:37:08.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Was it not a happy marriage, then?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:09.61,0:37:11.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was strained.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:12.53,0:37:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He wanted an heir.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:13.86,0:37:15.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She wanted a child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.32,0:37:19.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She kept trying{\i0}\N{\i1}long after the doctors warned her not to.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:19.87,0:37:23.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Every month when her courses came,{\i0}\N{\i1}it broke my heart to see her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:24.83,0:37:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She was lucky to have you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.50,0:37:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Everyone talked{\i0}\N{\i1}as though it was her fault.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.54,0:37:31.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But how could they know that?{\i0}\N{\i1}It is not always the woman who is barren.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.05,0:37:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sometimes{\i0}\N{\i1}it is the man's fault, of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.22,0:37:37.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh dear.{\i0}\N{\i1}I am afraid I am speaking out of turn.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:38.01,0:37:40.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No. Not at all, Mrs. Colson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:41.10,0:37:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.97,0:37:43.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You were saying?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:44.93,0:37:48.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I said to the duchess{\i0}\N{\i1}what my mother said to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:49.23,0:37:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A womb cannot quicken{\i0}\N{\i1}without strong, healthy seed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.86,0:37:56.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And then, just as she was finally blessed{\i0}\N{\i1}with Master Simon…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.36,0:37:58.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sobbing] we lost her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:02.70,0:38:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[knocking at door]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:06.50,0:38:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why are you not dressed?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.83,0:38:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I told you we were dining{\i0}\N{\i1}with Lady Gartside this evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:10.63,0:38:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[coughing, gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.84,0:38:14.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sorry, Mama. I'm not feeling well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:15.38,0:38:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I ought to make you come along{\i0}\N{\i1}to cough and splutter all evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.68,0:38:20.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It would serve Lady Gartside right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.72,0:38:24.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She has been withholding{\i0}\N{\i1}a dinner invitation from me, and now look…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.10,0:38:27.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not a day{\i0}\N{\i1}after Miss Thompson's announcement,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.39,0:38:29.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and they all come crawling.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:29.40,0:38:30.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[coughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.44,0:38:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Enjoy your evening, Mama!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.11,0:38:34.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[footsteps receding]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.99,0:38:37.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.65,0:38:39.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.87,0:38:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathes deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.74,0:38:44.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[suspenseful music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.21,0:38:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[suspenseful music continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:36.42,0:39:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[suspenseful music intensifies]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:03.53,0:40:05.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[suspenseful music ends]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.87,0:40:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Penelope, what are you…?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.67,0:40:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-How dare you!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Look.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.96,0:40:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look at the signature{\i0}\N{\i1}on Sir George's last letter,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.25,0:40:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and this one from many months ago.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.92,0:40:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-So?{\i0}\N{\i1}-So, they are not the same.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.34,0:40:25.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The slant of the lettering,{\i0}\N{\i1}it is all wrong.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:25.76,0:40:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Penelope, I'm tired. I haven't--{\i0}\N{\i1}-This one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:29.52,0:40:31.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was in a drawer{\i0}\N{\i1}on the back of Mama's desk.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.52,0:40:35.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She or even Mrs. Varley{\i0}\N{\i1}practiced George's signature,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:35.98,0:40:37.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but even they could not get it perfect.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:37.94,0:40:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That last letter,{\i0}\N{\i1}the one where he broke your heart…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:42.36,0:40:44.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it was a forgery, Marina.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:45.20,0:40:47.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}George never wrote those things to you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:47.28,0:40:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He never denied loving you.{\i0}\N{\i1}He never denied your child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.54,0:40:52.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Perhaps.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Marina--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.16,0:40:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Even if you are correct--{\i0}\N{\i1}-I am correct. You cannot deny--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:54.92,0:40:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even if it is true, George has{\i0}\N{\i1}still not replied to my letters.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:58.34,0:41:00.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He has abandoned me,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.59,0:41:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}while Colin has embraced me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.47,0:41:03.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought you loved him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:04.97,0:41:05.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}George.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:06.55,0:41:07.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was a fool.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.30,0:41:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This changes nothing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.52,0:41:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why is your bag packed?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:23.15,0:41:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell me you are not going to Gretna Green!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.91,0:41:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina! What will you do{\i0}\N{\i1}when Colin realizes the child is not his?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.16,0:41:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That day will come. He is not simple.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.95,0:41:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What I will do{\i0}\N{\i1}is live safe in the knowledge{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:36.29,0:41:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that my husband is a good and kind man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.58,0:41:41.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He would never turn me out on the street.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.13,0:41:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He will care for us both, come what may.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:44.80,0:41:46.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But what of him? What of Colin?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:50.35,0:41:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You love him.{\i0}\N{\i1}-What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:52.52,0:41:55.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, it makes sense now.{\i0}\N{\i1}Your objections, your meddling.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.56,0:41:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You love Colin Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.19,0:41:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know not of what you speak.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.06,0:42:01.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe I know{\i0}\N{\i1}so much more than you, Pen…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.98,0:42:04.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of Colin, of the world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:04.99,0:42:08.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I am to be the executioner{\i0}\N{\i1}of this childish infatuation,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:08.16,0:42:09.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}then so be it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:10.82,0:42:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your love is an unrequited fantasy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.25,0:42:15.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Colin sees you as you are{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:15.58,0:42:18.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and regards you no differently{\i0}\N{\i1}than he does Eloise,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:18.67,0:42:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or even little Hyacinth.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:21.13,0:42:23.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He sees me as a wife, a woman.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:23.75,0:42:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And as a woman,{\i0}\N{\i1}I must make these difficult choices{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.67,0:42:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for myself and for my child…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:31.89,0:42:33.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}even if they hurt your feelings.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:40.27,0:42:42.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens, closes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:53.12,0:42:54.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Working late, Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.37,0:42:57.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Curse it. What time is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:59.67,0:43:00.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.25,0:43:04.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}These books seem{\i0}\N{\i1}to have taken possession of you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:05.00,0:43:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Those people rely on me to make a living,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.01,0:43:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to feed their families.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.88,0:43:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should not have stayed away so long.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.80,0:43:13.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why did you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.93,0:43:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No particular reason.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:15.76,0:43:16.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Business in London.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.43,0:43:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But then I met this impertinent young lady{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.02,0:43:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with a right hook{\i0}\N{\i1}like an East End prizefighter.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.19,0:43:24.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am serious.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:24.69,0:43:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As am I.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:31.16,0:43:33.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Simon.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Daphne.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:42.37,0:43:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both breathing heavily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.21,0:43:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:50.59,0:43:52.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Daphne panting]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Simon grunting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:52.80,0:43:54.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne exclaims passionately]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.85,0:43:59.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:08.40,0:44:10.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[coins and books clatter]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:10.86,0:44:12.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon gasping urgently]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:17.91,0:44:19.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon exclaims, moans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:20.45,0:44:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhaling sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.00,0:44:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ah!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.25,0:44:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon panting loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:28.71,0:44:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-We ought to clean up for dinner.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:35.14,0:44:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll meet you in the dining room.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:38.97,0:44:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[ominous music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.19,0:44:45.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace!{\i0}\N{\i1}These are the servants' quarters!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.06,0:44:47.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where is Miss Nolan?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.57,0:44:53.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace, what is wrong?{\i0}\N{\i1}You should have rung for me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:54.03,0:44:56.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I need you to tell me something, Rose.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.20,0:44:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathing nervously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:59.24,0:45:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How does a woman come to be with child?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:02.62,0:45:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Y-Your mother--{\i0}\N{\i1}-My mother told me nothing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:07.21,0:45:10.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please. No embarrassment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.38,0:45:13.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Explain it to me, precisely.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:14.63,0:45:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[dramatic piano music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.39,0:45:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] {\i0}<span style="style2">It was such a simple solution.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:17.97,0:45:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[distant, echoing]{\i0}\N{\i1}We can increase the harvest{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.10,0:45:22.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if the farmers plant turnip.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:22.18,0:45:25.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}On my travels, I encountered farmers{\i0}\N{\i1}who tripled their income{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:25.23,0:45:29.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}by no longer rotating crops,{\i0}\N{\i1}and instead, planting turnip,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:29.23,0:45:32.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and then turning out sheep to graze{\i0}\N{\i1}and remove the weeds.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:39.74,0:45:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[dramatic piano music continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:01.64,0:46:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon grunts, sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.69,0:46:08.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne exhales deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:25.12,0:46:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Farmer Robert] {\i0}<span style="style2">Thank you, Your Grace!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:27.66,0:46:30.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And please send{\i0}\N{\i1}my great thanks to the duke!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.54,0:46:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He has purchased us{\i0}\N{\i1}several cattle for the farm{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:34.88,0:46:39.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so that we may rear livestock{\i0}\N{\i1}until the soil is fertile again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.59,0:46:42.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our fortunes have been restored. [laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.31,0:46:46.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.81,0:46:50.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You may return to the house.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:52.11,0:46:53.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wish to walk a while.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:15.84,0:47:17.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[dramatic piano music ends]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.51,0:47:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[clock ticking]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:33.61,0:47:35.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[footsteps approaching]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.65,0:47:37.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you ready for bed, my dear?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.90,0:47:40.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe I am.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:54.79,0:48:00.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Keep your breath on me ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.17,0:48:05.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ And keep keep keep going{\i0}\N{\i1}'Til my body is free ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:08.81,0:48:14.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ And keep keep keep going{\i0}\N{\i1}'Til my body is free ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:14.56,0:48:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.15,0:48:20.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Keep your eyes on me ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:25.03,0:48:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ And keep keep keep going{\i0}\N{\i1}'Til I'm the last thing you see ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.66,0:48:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:32.62,0:48:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Keep your touch on my skin ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:38.46,0:48:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:40.88,0:48:46.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Keep keep keep going{\i0}\N{\i1}Keep keep keep going ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.60,0:48:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ Oh you're taking me down{\i0}\N{\i1}Haunting my dreams ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.81,0:48:56.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ I'd like to end the world with you ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.40,0:49:00.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ You're taking me on{\i0}\N{\i1}Haunting my heart ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:00.28,0:49:03.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ I'm at the end of the world with you ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:04.24,0:49:08.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ You're taking me down{\i0}\N{\i1}Haunting my dreams ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:08.20,0:49:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[panting] Wait. Wait.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:10.29,0:49:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Daphne moans]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Daphne…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:13.79,0:49:14.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.96,0:49:15.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.04,0:49:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ I'm at the end of the world with you ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.96,0:49:21.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunting forcefully]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:25.72,0:49:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[panting slows]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:31.47,0:49:32.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both panting tremulously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.81,0:49:33.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.69,0:49:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:41.07,0:49:42.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.40,0:49:45.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[panting] Daphne.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.70,0:49:46.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:50.49,0:49:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wh-Wh-What…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.99,0:49:53.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What did you do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.87,0:49:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had hoped it was not true.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:56.62,0:49:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had hoped I was mistaken,{\i0}\N{\i1}but clearly, I was not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:59.88,0:50:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-How could you?{\i0}\N{\i1}-How could I?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.38,0:50:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How could {\i0}<span style="style2">I?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:03.96,0:50:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You lied to me.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I did not lie.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.01,0:50:06.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I trusted you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:07.59,0:50:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I trusted you{\i0}\N{\i1}more than anyone in this world,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:10.80,0:50:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you took advantage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:12.35,0:50:15.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You seized an opportunity.{\i0}\N{\i1}And so I did the very same.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:15.18,0:50:17.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I told you I cannot give you children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:17.19,0:50:21.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Cannot" and "will not"{\i0}\N{\i1}are two entirely different things.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:21.90,0:50:23.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You chose this for yourself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:23.98,0:50:25.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You chose to lie to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:25.15,0:50:26.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not lie.{\i0}\N{\i1}I thought you were prepared.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:27.07,0:50:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought you understood{\i0}\N{\i1}how a child came to be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.07,0:50:33.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You took my future from me,{\i0}\N{\i1}the one thing I wanted more than anything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:33.29,0:50:35.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You knew.{\i0}\N{\i1}You knew that becoming a mother,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.54,0:50:37.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to have a family of my own one day,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.37,0:50:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you knew that was all I ever wanted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.17,0:50:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was prepared{\i0}\N{\i1}to die on that dueling field{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:42.25,0:50:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}rather than marry you{\i0}\N{\i1}and take your dream away.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.55,0:50:46.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would have died for you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:46.30,0:50:48.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You were the one{\i0}\N{\i1}who insisted on this union.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.43,0:50:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You told me I was enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.22,0:50:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That was before I knew you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:53.56,0:50:56.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you know, I even felt pity for you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.10,0:50:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Poor Simon," I thought.{\i0}\N{\i1}"How it must pain him{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:58.89,0:51:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to never know{\i0}\N{\i1}what it is to be a father."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:00.85,0:51:03.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I never asked for your pity.{\i0}\N{\i1}-And I never asked for your betrayal!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.61,0:51:06.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Daphne, I--{\i0}\N{\i1}-You what?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:08.40,0:51:09.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You what?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.74,0:51:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You love me?{\i0}\N{\i1}No, you most certainly do not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:13.53,0:51:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not know the meaning of the word.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:16.50,0:51:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not lie to the one you love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:18.66,0:51:20.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not trick the one you love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:20.46,0:51:23.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not humiliate the one you love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:23.75,0:51:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I may not know much,{\i0}\N{\i1}as you have made abundantly clear,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:27.26,0:51:28.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I do know one thing…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:28.55,0:51:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know {\i0}<span style="style2">that {\i0}{\i1}is not love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:39.48,0:51:40.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:41.02,0:51:44.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">All is fair in love and war,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:45.23,0:51:47.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but some battles leave no victor,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.53,0:51:50.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}only a trail of broken hearts{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.99,0:51:53.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that makes us wonder if the price we pay{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:53.74,0:51:55.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is ever worth the fight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:00.62,0:52:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:02.79,0:52:07.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The ones we love have the power{\i0}\N{\i1}to inflict the greatest scars.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:08.71,0:52:11.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For what thing is more fragile…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:12.09,0:52:13.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}than the human heart?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.43,0:52:16.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sobbing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:24.69,0:52:25.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise] Shh.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:35.41,0:52:40.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown] {\i0}<span style="style2">The bond{\i0}\N<span style="style2">between man and bride is private, sacred.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:41.75,0:52:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I must tell you,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.71,0:52:47.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have learned{\i0}\N{\i1}that a grave fraud is afoot.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:47.96,0:52:49.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.97,0:53:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As if the Featheringtons{\i0}\N{\i1}did not have enough to be dealing with,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:02.85,0:53:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Marina Thompson is with child…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:11.99,0:53:16.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and she has been from the very first day{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.24,0:53:18.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}she arrived in our fair city.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:28.08,0:53:32.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Desperate times may call{\i0}\N{\i1}for desperate measures,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.17,0:53:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I would wager many will think{\i0}\N{\i1}her actions beyond the pale.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:38.47,0:53:41.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps she thought it her only option,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:41.35,0:53:44.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or perhaps she knows no shame.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:45.19,0:53:46.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I ask you,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:46.39,0:53:50.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}can the ends ever justify{\i0}\N{\i1}such wretched means?{\i0}
